      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sounds like a profound exhaustion—not just of the body, but of the spirit. When the future is just a corridor of empty hours, the waiting becomes its own kind of prison. You don't need permission to exist; you need permission to feel that this is real. And if nothing else, I see that you're still here, still speaking, still reaching out.",
